<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreigners hold 59.2 pct of NZ govt securities.</title>
<headline>Foreigners hold 59.2 pct of NZ govt securities.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners fell in May to 59.2 percent from 61.9 percent in April, the Reserve Bank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>			   May 1997	   Apr 1997	   May 1996</p>
<p>Bills &amp; Bonds	 Value Pct(*)     Value Pct(*)    Value Pct(*)</p>
<p>T Bills		3,323.6 54.5	3,169.7 49.3    3,428.6 46.7</p>
<p>Govt Bonds	  11,166.5 60.8     12,150.7 66.3   10,719.4 53.5</p>
<p>Total Securities  14,490.1 59.2     15,320.4 61.9   14,148.0 51.6</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds</p>
<p>07/97		    649.1 42.2	  707.4 44.0	949.2 48.4</p>
<p>07/98		    966.3 39.5	1,544.8 63.1    1,463.8 59.8</p>
<p>02/00		  1,937.3 64.3	2,008.3 66.7    1,305.1 43.3</p>
<p>02/01		  1,498.6 62.4	1,652.7 71.9	979.1 66.4</p>
<p>03/02		  1,474.8 58.7	1,626.8 64.8    1,198.6 47.7</p>
<p>04/04		  2,124.7 69.8	2,084.6 68.5    1,914.5 62.9</p>
<p>11/06		  2,199.4 79.2	2,239.5 80.6    1,455.0 57.0</p>
<p>02/16		    316.3 58.5	  286.6 53.3	 38.2 19.1</p>
<p>(*) Percentages represent non-resident holdings as a percentage of total securities in hand of market, excluding RBNZ/Treasury holdings.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
